========================================
          BASIC GIT COMMAND FLOW
========================================

1. FIRST-TIME GIT CONFIGURATION
--------------------------------

git config --global user.name "Your Name"
git config --global user.email "your@email.com"

Check configuration:
git config --list


2. CREATE A GIT REPOSITORY
--------------------------

Go inside your project folder:

git init

Check status:
git status


3. CONNECT PROJECT TO GITHUB
----------------------------

git remote add origin https://github.com/username/repository.git

Check remote:
git remote -v


4. CHECK BRANCHES
-----------------

Local branches:
git branch

Remote branches:
git branch -r

All branches:
git branch -a


5. CREATE A NEW BRANCH
----------------------

Create + switch:
git switch -c feature-name

Check current branch:
git branch


6. WORK ON YOUR CODE
--------------------

Create / modify / delete files.

Check changes:
git status

See changes:
git diff


7. STAGE CHANGES
----------------

Stage one file:
git add filename.py

Stage all changes:
git add .


8. COMMIT CHANGES
-----------------

git commit -m "Describe your changes"

Check commit history:
git log

Short commit history:
git log --oneline


9. PUSH TO GITHUB
-----------------

First time pushing a new branch:
git push -u origin feature-name

After upstream is set:
git push

For main:
git push -u origin main


10. GET CHANGES FROM GITHUB
---------------------------

Fetch remote changes:
git fetch

Get + integrate remote changes:
git pull


11. SWITCH BRANCH
-----------------

Switch to existing branch:
git switch main

Switch to feature branch:
git switch feature-name


12. MERGE A BRANCH
------------------

Go to the branch you want to merge INTO:

git switch main

Get latest changes:
git pull

Merge feature branch:
git merge feature-name

Push merged changes:
git push


13. DELETE LOCAL BRANCH
-----------------------

First switch to another branch:

git switch main

Delete branch:
git branch -d feature-name


14. DELETE REMOTE BRANCH
------------------------

git push origin --delete feature-name


15. RENAME BRANCH
-----------------

Rename current branch:
git branch -m new-name

Example:
git branch -m development


16. RESTORE / DISCARD CHANGES
-----------------------------

Restore a modified file:
git restore filename.py

Unstage a file:
git restore --staged filename.py


17. VIEW COMMIT HISTORY
-----------------------

Full history:
git log

Short history:
git log --oneline

Graph:
git log --oneline --graph --all


18. VIEW DIFFERENCES
--------------------

Unstaged changes:
git diff

Staged changes:
git diff --staged


19. CLONE EXISTING GITHUB REPOSITORY
------------------------------------

git clone https://github.com/username/repository.git

Go inside project:
cd repository

Check:
git status


========================================
       NORMAL DAILY GIT WORKFLOW
========================================

git switch main
git pull

# Create feature branch
git switch -c feature-name

# Work on your code...

git status
git add .
git commit -m "Add feature"

# Push feature branch
git push -u origin feature-name

# After feature is completed
git switch main
git pull
git merge feature-name
git push

# Delete feature branch
git branch -d feature-name
git push origin --delete feature-name


